Pre-existing bug, NOT caused by NEARS-3088 (file not in this ticket's diff; unchanged since base
commit 6d005c4a0).

GET /admin/business-settings/system-addon (as authenticated admin) -> HTTP 500

storage/logs/laravel.log:
[2026-09-06 14:18:13] production.ERROR: [FAIL] scandir(Modules): Failed to open directory: No
such file or directory {"correlation_id":"547ba12e-5a58-48ae-a71c-7fe85a2ed85e",
"type":"ErrorException","endpoint":"/admin/business-settings/system-addon"}

Root cause: App\Http\Controllers\Admin\System\AddonController::index() does
    $dir = 'Modules';           // RELATIVE path
    $directories = self::getDirectories($dir);   // scandir($dir) internally
`php artisan serve` (and the plain `php -S ... server.php` it wraps) runs the actual PHP
built-in webserver with its CWD set to Admin/public/, not Admin/ -- verified live:
    $ lsof -p <serve-child-pid> | grep cwd
    php ... cwd DIR ... /Users/Apple/Projects/nears-worktrees/NEARS-3088/Admin/public
So the relative 'Modules' resolves to Admin/public/Modules, which does not exist (the real
Modules/ dir lives at Admin/Modules/, one level up) -- scandir() throws ErrorException on ANY
request-served process using the built-in dev server, regardless of what modules_statuses.json
says or whether Rental/Gateways are enabled/disabled/absent.

Confirmed unrelated to this diff: app/Http/Controllers/Admin/System/AddonController.php is not
among NEARS-3088's 22 modified + 2 new files, and the relative-path scandir() call predates this
ticket. Filed as a regression-candidate followup, not a NEARS-3088 finding.
